  "body": "Cause: the test `troubleshooting_messages_still_exist_in_the_sources` joins string literals that continue on the next line with a backslash. It split on backslash plus LF. On a checkout with `core.autocrlf=true` the line end is CRLF, so the join did not match and the message stem was not found. LF checkouts and the runners were green.\n\nThe change (test code only, `crates/app/tests/docs_troubleshooting.rs`):\n- New helper `normalise_eol` replaces CRLF with LF.\n- The join code is now the helper `join_continuations`, which calls `normalise_eol` first. The sources go through it.\n- The docs page text goes through `normalise_eol` too.\n- No assert and no stem changed.\n- New test `join_continuations_accepts_crlf_line_ends` pins the fix.\n\nRed-first evidence: the new test was run with the `normalise_eol` call in `join_continuations` disabled. It failed with \"CRLF continuation was not joined\". With the call restored, both tests pass.\n\nCRLF-file run: `crates/sim/src/verify/types.rs` (it holds backslash-continued refusal strings) was converted to CRLF on disk only. `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test docs_troubleshooting -j 6` gave 2 passed, 0 failed. The file was then restored with `git checkout`.\n\nCommands run:\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test docs_troubleshooting -j 6`\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --test docs_troubleshooting -j 6 -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\nNot run: the batch and release gates, and any test on a real `core.autocrlf=true` checkout (the reporter is asked to run it).\n\nNo product code changes.\n\nEffort: low\nChangelog: none\n\nFixes #3619\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
